FOR HIDDE: apply this by hand, or in any session/token that has the
`workflow` GitHub scope. This bot's push token does not, confirmed again
2026-09-13 (same wall reported 2026-09-09): GitHub refuses any push that
touches a file under .github/workflows/* without it, even bundled with
other, unrelated changes, so this cannot be committed directly no matter
how it is split.

WHAT: adds the retry flag to the iOS "floor" job (iOS 18 only) that the
"test" job (newest iOS) has always had. Without it, a genuinely flaky UI
test (one slow cold-launch tap into a MapKit-backed sheet, or a slow
search debounce) fails the whole scheduled run outright, twice now on
2026-09-12, even though the identical suite passes reliably on the newest
runtime job right next to it. `testEveryFlowLeavesAWayBack` in
FlowWalk.swift and `testSearchingForATreeMovesTheMapToIt` in
AncientTreesUITests.swift both carry code comments pointing at this patch.

HOW TO APPLY, from the repo root:
    git apply drafts/ios-floor-retry.patch
    git rm drafts/ios-floor-retry.patch
    git add .github/workflows/ios.yml
    git commit -m "iOS floor job: add the retry flag the test job already has"
    git push

Or just make this one-line change by hand in .github/workflows/ios.yml,
in the "Build and test on the floor" step, so the floor job's xcodebuild
call matches the test job's:

--- a/.github/workflows/ios.yml
+++ b/.github/workflows/ios.yml
@@ -493,6 +493,7 @@ jobs:
             -scheme AncientTrees \
             -destination "id=$UDID" \
             -derivedDataPath /tmp/dd \
+            -retry-tests-on-failure -test-iterations 2 \
             -parallel-testing-enabled NO \
             -skip-testing:AncientTreesUITests/SweepFrames \
             -skip-testing:AncientTreesUITests/RefusedWalk \
